# Agent routing

## Available agents

- `@architect` — Principal architect — design decisions, ADRs, planning, scoping, and team coordination.
- `@atlas` — Telegram/GitHub relay agent — classifies inter-team messages and routes to Neo or Vera. Does not make delivery decisions.
- `@builder` — Principal engineer — implementation, tests, PRs, and QA handoff.
- `@neo` — Principal engineer for SETCHIN delivery — tickets, code review, architecture, BD drafts, and QA handoff.
- `@router` — Inter-team relay agent — classifies inbound messages and routes to Architect, Builder, or Tester. Does not make delivery decisions.
- `@tester` — Independent QA engineer — black-box verification, pass/fail evidence, defect reporting.
- `@vera` — Independent QA engineer — black-box verification against acceptance criteria, pass/fail evidence, defect reporting.

## Invocation

This hub folder must be open in your Cursor workspace for `@architect` to resolve.

```
@architect  Read .cursor/agents/architect.md. Then read memory/architect.md. Then: you are in architecture mode. Review <project>...
@builder    Read .cursor/agents/builder.md. Then read memory/builder.md. Then: implement projects/<project>/task_N_todo_<slug>.md
@tester     Read .cursor/agents/tester.md. Then read memory/tester.md. Then: QA projects/<project>/task_N_todo_<slug>.md
@router     Read .cursor/agents/router.md. Then read memory/router.md. Then: classify and route: [inbound message]
```

If the short name doesn't resolve (hub folder not in workspace, not yet indexed), use the explicit file path:

```
@.cursor/agents/architect.md  Read .cursor/agents/architect.md. Then read memory/architect.md. Then: you are in architecture mode. Review <project>...
@.cursor/agents/builder.md    Read .cursor/agents/builder.md. Then read memory/builder.md. Then: implement projects/<project>/task_N_todo_<slug>.md
@.cursor/agents/tester.md     Read .cursor/agents/tester.md. Then read memory/tester.md. Then: QA projects/<project>/task_N_todo_<slug>.md
@.cursor/agents/router.md     Read .cursor/agents/router.md. Then read memory/router.md. Then: classify and route: [inbound message]
```

## Task queue

- Current task: `npm run dispatch -- <project>`
- Advance: `npm run advance -- <project>`
- All pending tasks: `npm run list`
